## BACKGROUND & CONTEXT

Memory management is a critical operational concern for long-running web scraping processes that can operate for hours or days, processing millions of pages and accumulating large datasets. Without proper memory monitoring, scrapers are susceptible to OutOfMemoryException crashes that corrupt crawls, lose progress, and require manual intervention. Memory leaks are particularly insidious in web scraping due to the accumulation of: response bodies, extracted items, URL queues, statistics counters, and cached data. Scrapy's MemoryUsageExtension provides real-time memory monitoring with configurable thresholds and automatic action triggers, allowing spiders to gracefully handle memory pressure rather than crashing. For Ghost, implementing comprehensive memory monitoring is essential for production reliability—production crawls cannot afford unplanned termination, and memory issues often manifest only after extended runtime when accumulated state reaches critical mass. This extension enables proactive memory management through configurable limits, automatic cleanup triggers, and graceful degradation rather than hard failures.

## SCRAPY ANALYSIS

Scrapy's MemoryUsageExtension monitors memory consumption using platform-specific APIs and triggers actions when thresholds are exceeded. Key features include: Configurable memory limits (MEMUSAGE_LIMIT_MB) defining maximum allowed memory; Warning threshold (MEMUSAGE_WARNING_MB) for early notification; Automatic spider shutdown when memory limit exceeded; Notification callbacks for memory threshold breaches; Periodic memory checking at configurable intervals; and Integration with engine signals for lifecycle management. The extension runs a background task that periodically samples memory usage via platform APIs (psutil on Python), compares against configured limits, and triggers configured actions (warnings, shutdowns, or custom callbacks). The shutdown process is cooperative, allowing pending items to complete processing before termination. Memory reporting includes current usage, peak usage, and process-wide statistics.

## GHOST INTEGRATION

This feature implements an Extension following Ghost's extension pattern, integrating with the signal system. Integration points include: (1) MemoryUsageExtension implementing IExtension with lifecycle management; (2) Signal system subscription to EngineStarted and EngineStopped events; (3) Periodic timer or background service for memory sampling; (4) Spider integration for graceful shutdown notification; (5) Stats collection reporting memory metrics; (6) Configuration system with MemoryMonitorConfiguration for thresholds; (7) Logging integration for memory threshold alerts; (8) Optional integration with AutoThrottle for coordinated slowdown under memory pressure. The extension will use .NET's GC and Process APIs for cross-platform memory monitoring without external dependencies.

