## IMPLEMENTATION NOTES

- Use reflection to discover contract attributes on spider methods at startup
- Implement ContractRunner as a hosted service that can be invoked via CLI or test framework
- Response caching should use consistent hashing of URL + headers to generate cache keys
- Support for mocking HTTP responses using recorded fixtures stored as JSON files
- Field validation should use reflection to compare actual item properties with contract expectations
- Implement contract inheritance by scanning base classes and aggregating contracts
- Parallel execution should use Parallel.ForEach or async Task.WhenAll with semaphore for throttling
- Integration with xUnit through custom test discoverer that finds contract attributes and generates test cases
- Support for custom validators by instantiating ValidatorType and calling IContractValidator.ValidateAsync
- Implement contract coverage analysis by tracking which spider methods have contracts vs. total methods
- Error reporting should include stack traces, response snapshots, and detailed diffs for debugging
- Support for contract versioning to handle website changes over time

## TESTING STRATEGY

- Unit tests: Verify contract attribute discovery and parsing from spider classes
- Validation tests: Verify field presence, type checking, and custom validator execution
- Caching tests: Verify responses are cached and reused correctly with TTL expiration
- Parallel execution tests: Verify concurrent contract execution doesn't cause race conditions
- Integration tests: End-to-end test running contracts against sample spiders with real URLs
- xUnit integration tests: Verify contracts are discovered and executed as part of test suites
- Coverage tests: Verify contract coverage reporting identifies spiders without test coverage
- Error handling tests: Verify graceful handling of network failures, timeouts, and malformed responses
- Edge case tests: Empty spiders, spiders with no contracts, circular contract references
- Performance tests: Measure contract execution time and memory usage with 100+ contracts
- Contract inheritance tests: Verify base class contracts are inherited and can be overridden

